    "lawCode": "Add §29-f, Veterans' Services L",
    "lawSection": "Veterans' Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7708\n\nSPONSOR: FERNANDEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the veterans' services law, in relation to the estab-\nlishing a veterans' bill of rights\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe department shall establish, print, publish and distribute a veter-\nans' bill of rights.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1  of  the  bill  amends the veterans' services law by adding\nsection 29c which  mandates  the  department  to  create,  publish,  and\ndistribute  a  comprehensive veterans' bill of rights. rights that state\nthe benefits, assistance, and expectations of treatment veterans  should\nreceive.\n\n  Section  2  provides  that  the  bill  is  to be made available on the\ndepartment's website and states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVeterans have sacrificed for our country and deserve to  understand  the\nrights and entitlements that result from their service. This bill serves\nto  delineate  the  benefits  available  to veterans through local state\nveterans' agencies, and to specify the rights that veterans hold. Clear-\nly stating the rights of our veterans in an easily  accessible  bill  is\nthe least we can do to honor those who have fought for our rights.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis  act  shall  take  effect  on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
